From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manos Koukoutos <manoskouk@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:17:36 +0000
Subject: [M156] [turbofan] Emit dedicated operator for trusted-pointer loads

Original change's description:
> [turbofan] Emit dedicated operator for trusted-pointer loads
>
> Instead of emitting a trusted-pointer load as a series of instructions
> in WasmGraphAssembler::BuildDecodeTrustedPointer, we emit a dedicated
> operator for it (LoadTrustedPointerOperator), which is translated into
> Turboshaft and then lowered in the instruction selector. This prevents
> load elimination from erroneously eliminating the load to the pointer
> handle.
>
> Fixed: 573378812
> Change-Id: Ic651fe29cec26aa4b23039db481dee6dcabcb5c6
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8591942
> Reviewed-by: Jakob Kummerow <jkummerow@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Manos Koukoutos <manoskouk@chromium.org>
> Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#110863}

(cherry picked from commit d4374eaec817692d144b16ade997040e60ee6139)

